Subject: [PATCH] fix(admin): the answer-record fixture can file under the
 goal's own field (1691)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ops 02:36Z, after the first wave-ranking read on goal 23926: the ranking read
its rates under „saklsi elektro gakvaniloba", and the tester's earlier
records sat under „elektrikosi saklsi gakvanilobis".

The asks and the ranking agree: both take the field from the goal's title.
Live, every ask of 23926 is filed under the ranking's field. The fixture
took it from the text the tester typed, and the title is the model's
wording of that text, so the two can differ. On top of that, the recount
after each ask rebuilds a record from the real asks, so a read after the
sends sees only those (asked 1 / yes 0, the 0.333 on all five).

The fixture now also takes task_id. The record goes under that goal's own
title field, for a goal on a fictional seat only (403 otherwise). goal_text
still works as before.

The order of steps for the tester: open the goal; on the plan card, set
each candidate's record with task_id; read GET
/admin/goals/:id/wave-ranking; only then approve.

DONE WHEN: records set with task_id show in the ranking's field_rate, and
the ranking orders the candidates by them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
